From 47cd598333f7d2a399c0b5dacd3e1f8be8e2e7cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:23:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add M5StickT2 board with FLIR Lepton 3.0
 thermal model

M5StickT2 (K016-T2) is the classic-ESP32 thermal-camera variant of the
StickC: ESP32-PICO-D4, 4 MiB flash, ST7789 135x240 panel, AXP192/PCF8563/
MPU6886 on the shared G21/G22 bus, and a FLIR Lepton 3.0 (160x120,
I2C CCI + SPI VoSPI) on SCK G2 / MISO G25 / CS G0 / VSYNC G38 /
RESET G26 with CCI at I2C 0x2A.  The official M5-StickT example also reads
an external I2C encoder at 0x30 (documented PA2/PA3/PA4 pin names do not
exist on the PICO-D4); the model follows the example.

New objects:
- m5stickt2 machine and board glue reusing the classic ESP32 SoC, the
  ST7789 board panel model (VSPI, DC G23) and the G21/G22 soft-I2C bridge;
- FLIR Lepton 3.0 model (hw/m5stopwatch/m5_lepton.c): a transfer-driven
  VoSPI stream of 164-byte packets (segment/line header, 80 big-endian
  pixels, CRC field carried as zero because the official driver reads and
  ignores it), 4 segments x 60 packets per deterministic synthetic 160x120
  thermal frame selected by frame-seed, VSYNC pulses at segment boundaries,
  RESET pin handling and QOM counters/digest;
- Lepton CCI model in the I2C slave device: 16-bit register addresses and
  16-bit data words with command execution for PING, FLIR serial number,
  FPA/AUX temperature and OEM sync SET commands;
- encoder 0x30 model: pointer 0x10 switch, pointer 0x00 big-endian delta and
  pointer 0x20 delta clear, with QOM-injectable increment/switch;
- a generic classic-ESP32 SPI slave attachment (esp32_spi_attach_spi_slave)
  so the VoSPI model can answer USR transactions while the guest drives the
  chip select through a GPIO;
- classic UART TX_DONE is now latched and cleared by INT_CLR instead of
  being derived from the TX FIFO level, which is required by the Arduino-
  ESP32 1.0.4/IDF v3 UART driver used by the official StickT2 demo (the
  previous level-derived bit produced a permanent level interrupt).

Guest evidence: the committed bare-metal probe
(tests/uiflow2/stickt2_probe) boots on this machine, receives three VoSPI
frames whose guest FNV-1a digests match the host fixture oracle for seeds
0/1/2 with zero packet errors, answers every CCI command, renders the frame
to the ST7789 panel (135x240 screenshot) and reads back a QOM-injected
encoder delta.  The official M5Burner "StickT2 User Demo" now reaches its
app boot marker under deterministic icount but its thermal/UI path is not
reached; physical optics/thermals remain NOT RUN.
---
